SYMBOLIC OBJECT  
 
Symbolic objects almost never exist alone in è  because alone they have almost no ability to 
refer to  something else. A web of objects, related by some kind of  guiding principle, can form a deep, 
complex pattern of  meaning, usually in support ¡ theme.  
When creating a web of symbolic objects, begin by  going back to th e designing principle ¦. 
