You can create  a web of symbolic objects in any story,  but ầ easiest ẩ in certain story 
forms, especially  myth, horror, and Western. These genre's have been written  so many times ¶y 
have been honed to perfection.  That includes objects that have been u sed so often ¶y  have 
ą recognizable metaphors. They are  prefabricated symbols whose meaning ®  
understands immediately at some level of conscious  thought.  
Let's ı the web of symbolic objects in some stories  that best represent t hese highly 
metaphorical genres.  
 
